IN PROGRESS (the builder's interim report; not yet in files):
- A new module lem/model/arm_consistency.py: the geometry contract, the torch readings and the loss. It hooks in beside body_tenure under its own loss key.
- Flags: --arm-consistency off|on (default off) and --arm-consistency-weight (default 0.0). Then the design note and the check program.
- Forearm-to-hand: the builder proposes a conservative bound. The hand origin stays inside a ball around its rest offset in the lower-arm frame, with radius equal to the sum over the wrist hinges of 2 x the anchor's distance from that hinge's axis. That holds for any wrist angle, soft-limit excursions included. It goes to independent review.
- The elbow-range penalty is omitted (soft limits have no valid bound); the elbow angle stays a logged reading only.
- Geometry route, as the hand geometry does:
  - a world command arm_geometry builds it from the compiled model;
  - with the flag on, the trainer asks every world once at launch and refuses if they disagree;
  - the learner checks the contract version, the handle names and the sha256 against a required --arm-consistency-geometry-sha256;
  - the flag on without geometry makes the lesson raise.

BLOCKER: the addendum's replay of the saved HEAD INPUTS is not possible from the a2 records as asked.
- What the captures hold: the command the head read (cap<step>_forecast_pose__iteration0_order and __selected_order, 8 x 26 x 9) and the achieved pose (cap<step>_decision__achieved, 8 x 26 x 10).
- What they lack: the head's latent input. In the capture file checked (chunk_000496261_3716_00004.npz, 89 keys), no key names a latent.
- What exists instead is the forward model's input, the encoder tokens and the memory bias. Rebuilding the latent from them needs the full forward model at the capture-time weights, and those were not saved: only the 496,250 and 496,350 states were.
- What can be measured exactly from the saved arrays: both terms' gradients in output space, and the last layer's per-example gradient norm ratio and cosine. The hidden activations cancel there.
- Your choice:
  (a) report the parameter-gradient comparison at the last layer only;
  (b) rebuild the latent from the saved tokens with the 496,350 weights: an approximation (not the capture-time weights) that needs a full forward-model load, beyond the efference-only load authorized;
  (c) a future capture that records the latent.
  The builder continues with everything else meanwhile.

